{
  "description": "General Maintenance: Rear Garden Garden entrance: North Western boundary: The trees on the boundary are growing within fairly close proximity of the building. \rT1: Sorbus: Approximately 5.00m: Tip prune by approximately 0.70m all round. Remove dead wood.\rT2: Purple Plum: Approximately 5.00m: Thin crown density evenly throughout by approximately 20%. Reduce back to previous points of reduction ensuring the retention of a natural crown profile with ample furnishing growth.\rT3 & T4: 2 x Winter Flowing Cherries: Approximately 5.00m: Remove deadwood throughout. Reduce crown by approximately 0.50m-0.70m, reducing wayward branches back into a compact crown form.\rMain Garden Area:\rT5-T6-T7: 3 x Multi stemmed Birch Trees: Approximately 14.00m: Thin crown densities of all by up to approximately 20% to increase light levels and reduce wind resistance.  Reduce extraneous branches which now protrude from the upper crown structure back to previous points of reduction, approximately 1.20m-1.40m to maintain compact crown profile whilst maintaining natural aspect. Crown raise to 4.00m.\rT8-T9-T10: 3 x Mature Limes:  Left hand boundary:  Reduce back to previous points of reduction. Thin crown density by 20% selecting suitable branch structure with furnishing growth, to reduce dimensions whilst preserving a natural crown shape. Remove dead wood throughout.",
